<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 29-day Cetes seen at 27.85 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 29-day Cetes seen at 27.85 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether one-month Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 83 basis points to 27.85 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    29-DAY     27.02	    27.85		   + 83 bps</p>
<p>    92-DAY     26.06	    26.50		   + 44 bps</p>
<p>    183-DAY    25.81	    25.83		   +  2 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.46	    25.51		   +  5 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>-- Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289554</p>
</text>
